# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WhatsApp engine + payout server — env config (copy to .env and fill in)
# P0 hardening 2026-07-27: NO credentials live in code anymore.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 🗄️ Legacy Mongo CRM routes (optional). The old hardcoded Atlas URI was
# committed to git — that password is BURNED: rotate it in Atlas before
# putting the new URI here. Leave unset to keep legacy routes disabled.
# MONGO_URI=mongodb://user:pass@host/...

# 🔐 Engine API shared secret (X-PT-Token). Unset = gate off — acceptable
# ONLY because the engine now binds to 127.0.0.1. Set it (and the matching
# VITE_WA_ENGINE_TOKEN in the frontend .env) before any network exposure.
# Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# WA_ENGINE_TOKEN=

# 🏦 Cashfree payout (payment-server.js). BOTH must be set or /api/payout
# answers 503. PAYOUT_ADMIN_KEY is the X-Admin-Key a caller must present —
# fail-closed: unset = payouts disabled.
# CASHFREE_CLIENT_ID=
# CASHFREE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# PAYOUT_ADMIN_KEY=

# 🛡️ SOC forwarding — where auth-failure events go (bridge /security/ingest).
# Default http://127.0.0.1:3000; token = one of the bridge's PT_BRIDGE_TOKEN
# values (unset works while the bridge gate is off in local dev).
# BRIDGE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
# PT_BRIDGE_TOKEN=

# 🔒 Bind address — DEFAULT loopback (127.0.0.1). Frontend calls
# http://localhost:5001 from this same PC, so nothing breaks. Only set
# HOST=0.0.0.0 for deliberate LAN exposure (and then SET WA_ENGINE_TOKEN).
# HOST=127.0.0.1

# 🤖 Gemini key for the legacy document scanner route (optional).
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Browser origins allowed by CORS (comma-separated) — defaults cover the
# prod domain + local dev; override only if you add a new frontend origin.
# WA_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
